From 489c98fb1b469b3539789f52b255f0fe8a9bfa0a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pranavi Somisetty <pranavi.somisetty@amd.com>
Date: Mon, 20 Jul 2026 23:58:15 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] lldp_util: use SIOCDEVPRIVATE+15 for Xilinx TSN NIC is_bridge
 ioctl

The Xilinx TSN NIC exposes its private ioctl at SIOCDEVPRIVATE+15
rather than the base SIOCDEVPRIVATE that openlldp's is_bridge() check
uses. Without this offset lldpad's bridge detection fails on the TSN
interface.

This is specific to the staging Xilinx TSN driver and is expected to be
dropped once the mainline TSN driver (currently under review) is used.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [staging Xilinx TSN driver-specific ioctl offset]

Signed-off-by: Pranavi Somisetty <pranavi.somisetty@amd.com>
---
 lldp_util.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/lldp_util.c b/lldp_util.c
index 61fb0bc..8e588fd 100644
--- a/lldp_util.c
+++ b/lldp_util.c
@@ -589,7 +589,7 @@ int is_bridge(const char *ifname)
 
 			ifr.ifr_data = (char *)args;
 			STRNCPY_TERMINATED(ifr.ifr_name, ifname, sizeof(ifr.ifr_name));
-			if (ioctl(fd, SIOCDEVPRIVATE, &ifr) == 0)
+			if (ioctl(fd, SIOCDEVPRIVATE+15, &ifr) == 0)
 				rc = 1;
 		}
 	}
-- 
